        "tekst": "The **course manual** lists as required reading **Giles, H. (2016). Communication Accommodation Theory**, a short entry (pp. 1-7) in the Wiley *International Encyclopedia of Communication Theory and Philosophy*.\n\nThe **slides** instead give **Dragojevic, Gasiorek & Giles (2016)**, a 24-page chapter in the Cambridge book, and cross out the older Giles & Ogay (2007) text.\n\nSame lead author, same year, same theory, but two different texts. They do not contradict each other: the encyclopedia entry is a short overview, the Cambridge chapter is the detailed version of the same ideas. This page is built on the Cambridge chapter (the one on the slides) and adds the overview elements from the encyclopedia entry and Giles & Ogay where they help. If you cite in an assignment, cite the text you actually used.\n\n**About the source text itself.** The full chapter sits behind a paywall and the author-uploaded copy could not be opened while building this page. The structure and examples here follow the chapter as published; details and wording are reconstructed from the chapter, the Giles & Ogay (2007) version of the theory, and the wider CAT literature. Treat names and years as reliable, but do not quote sentences from this page as if they were the book's words."
